RM Get Active Build Name From RM
    [Documentation]
    ...  Description:
    ...  KW sends command "SWmanShellCommand -i" to RM found by SN. Looks for line containing "activeBuildName".
    ...  If specific RegEx is fulfilled returns sw_version for RM.
    ...
    ...  +----------+------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Argument | Man.  | Description                                                  |
    ...  +==========+======+===============================================================+
    ...  | sn       | Yes   | SN of RM to ask for active build name                       |
    ...  +----------+------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...
    ...  Author: patryk.niewiejski@nokia.com
    ...  Maintainer: patryk.niewiejski@nokia.com
    [Arguments]  ${sn}
    radio.Open Connection To Radio Module  ${sn}
    radio.Send Command  SWmanShellCommand -i
    ${response}  radio.Read Until Prompt  $|#|>
    ${sw_version}  Get Regexp Matches  ${response}  \r\r\nactiveBuildName:\\s*(?P<sw_version>[A-Z0-9a-z._-]*)\\r\\r\\n  sw_version
    [Teardown]  radio.Close SSH Connection
    [Return]  ${sw_version[0]}

RM Verify Serial Number
    [Arguments]  ${serial_number}  ${connection}
    [Documentation]
    ...  KW checks if serial number given by user is visible on the RMODs list.
    ...  This list is generated by KW "Get Parameters For All  RMOD"
    ...  If SN is no visible on the BTS, test is set to Fail.
    ...  KW moved from robotlte_legacy and hran_ta: "Verify Serial Number"
    ...
    ...  | **Author:** mateusz.kawka@nokia.com
    ...  | **Maintainer:** lukasz.wystup@nokia.com
    ...
    ...  **Input Parameters:**
    ...
    ...  +------------------+------+-----------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Parameter        | Man. | Description                                         |
    ...  +==================+======+=====================================================+
    ...  | serial_number    | Yes  | Serial number of RMOD                               |
    ...  +------------------+------+-----------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | connection       | Yes  | current bts id as alias                             |
    ...  +------------------+------+-----------------------------------------------------+
    ...
    ...  Return:
    ...
    ...  Returns the RMOD object whose serial number matches the input.
    ...  If no match is found, the test fails with an appropriate error message.
    ...
    ...  **Example of simple usage:**
    ...
    ...  .. code-block:: robotframework
    ...
    ...     Verify Serial Number  K9175107169  connection=${BTS_ID}

    ${rmods}  admin.Get Parameters For All  RMOD  connection=${connection}
    FOR  ${rmod}  IN  @{rmods}
      Return From Keyword If  '${rmod.serialNumber}'=='${serial_number}'  ${rmod}
    END
    Fail  Serial Number ${serial_number} not found in HW Configuration! Test set to Fail!

RM Get Cells Mapping By RMOD Id
    [Arguments]  ${rat}  ${radio_id}  ${connection}
    [Documentation]
    ...  KW returns all cells for the specified technology (RAT) deployed on a given RMOD.
    ...  Unlike `Get Cell Mapping By Module ID`, this keyword correctly handles cells deployed
    ...  in chaining configurations. It was migrated from `robotlte_legacy` and `hran_ta` under
    ...  the original name: "Get Cells Mapping By RMOD Id".
    ...
    ...  | **Author:** mateusz.kawka@nokia.com
    ...  | **Maintainer:** lukasz.wystup@nokia.com
    ...
    ...  **Input Parameters:**
    ...  +------------------+------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Parameter        | Man. | Description                                                      |
    ...  +==================+======+==================================================================+
    ...  | rat              | Yes  | Supported values: GSM, WCDMA, LTE, NR. |
    ...  | radio_id         | Yes  | Full Radio ID path from runtime view.                            |
    ...  | connection       | Yes  | BTS ID used as alias for admin connection.                       |
    ...  +------------------+------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...
    ...  Return:
    ...  +-------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Return Value            | Description                                                      |
    ...  +=========================+==================================================================+
    ...  | list_of_cell            | List of internal cell IDs deployed on the given RMOD.            |
    ...  +-------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  **Example of simple usage:**
    ...
    ...  .. code-block:: robotframework
    ...
    ...  Get Cells Mapping By RMOD Id  rat=NR  radio_id=/MRBTS-1/RAT-1/RUNTIME_VIEW-1/MRBTS_R-1/EQM_R-1/APEQM_R-1/RMOD_R-3  connection=${BTS_ID}


    ${whole_list}  admin.Get Cell List  connection=${connection}

    ${rat_cells}  Evaluate  (${whole_list}\['cells']['${rat.lower()}'])

    ${ids_list}  Create List
    FOR  ${rat_cell}  IN  @{rat_cells}
        Run Keyword If  '${rat}'=='LTE'
        ...  Continue For Loop If  'iot' in '${rat_cell['technology'].lower()}'
        ${carriers_list}  Evaluate  (${rat_cell}\['carrierList'])
        ${status}  _RM Carrier List Iterator For Cells Mapping  ${carriers_list}  ${radio_id}
        Continue For Loop If  '${status}'=='False'
        ${cell_id}  Evaluate  (${rat_cell}\['id']['internal'])
        Append To List  ${ids_list}  ${cell_id}
    END

    ${list_of_cell}  Remove Duplicates  ${ids_list}

    [Return]  ${list_of_cell}

_RM Carrier List Iterator For Cells Mapping
    [Arguments]  ${carrier_list}  ${radio_id}
    [Documentation]
    ...  KW returns status True/False depending on whether any carrier in the provided list
    ...  is deployed on the specified RMOD. It compares RMOD identifiers extracted from
    ...  carrier antenna line IDs with the given radio ID.
    ...
    ...  | **Author:** mateusz.kawka@nokia.com
    ...  | **Maintainer:** lukasz.wystup@nokia.com
    ...
    ...  **Input Parameters:**
    ...  +------------------+------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Parameter        | Man. | Description                                                      |
    ...  +==================+======+==================================================================+
    ...  | carrier_list     | Yes  | List of carrier objects from the cell list.                      |
    ...  | radio_id         | Yes  | Full Radio ID from runtime view, used to match RMOD.             |
    ...  +------------------+------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...
    ...  Return:
    ...  +-------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Return Value            | Description                                                      |
    ...  +=========================+==================================================================+
    ...  | status                  | True if any carrier matches the given RMOD, otherwise False.     |
    ...  +-------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+

    FOR  ${carrier}  IN  @{carrier_list}
        ${antennaline}  Get From Dictionary  ${carrier}  antennaLineId
        ${rmod_id}  Evaluate  (${antennaline}\['internal'])
        ${rmod_id}  Evaluate  re.search(r'RMOD_R-\\d+', '${rmod_id}').group(0)  re
        ${radio_id}  Evaluate  re.search(r'RMOD_R-\\d+', '${radio_id}').group(0)  re
        ${status}  Set Variable If  '${rmod_id}'=='${radio_id}'  True  False
        Return From Keyword If  '${status}'=='True'  ${status}
    END

    [Return]  ${status}

RM Get RU Serial Number For DistName
    [Arguments]  ${rmod_id}  ${connection}
    [Documentation]
    ...  KW returns the RMOD serial number based on a given
    ...  RMOD DistName/ID. It fetches parameters for all RMOD objects from the specified connection,
    ...  finds the RMOD matching the provided `rmod_id`, and returns its `serialNumber` field.
    ...
    ...  | **Author:** mateusz.kawka@nokia.com
    ...  | **Maintainer:** lukasz.wystup@nokia.com
    ...
    ...  **Input Parameters:**
    ...
    ...  +------------------+------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Parameter        | Man. | Description                                                      |
    ...  +==================+======+==================================================================+
    ...  | rmod_id          | Yes  | RMOD DistName/ID                                                 |
    ...  | connection       | Yes  | Connection handle or node identifier (e.g., ${BTS_ID}).          |
    ...  +------------------+------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...
    ...  **Return:**
    ...  +-------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Return Value            | Description                                                      |
    ...  +=========================+==================================================================+
    ...  | ${rmod_sn}              | Serial number (string) of the matched RMOD/RU.                   |
    ...  | ${None}                 | If no RMOD with the given `rmod_id` is found.                    |
    ...  +-------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------+

    ${rmod_params}  admin.Get Parameters For All  class_name=RMOD  connection=${connection}
    FOR  ${rmod}  IN  @{rmod_params}
      Continue For Loop If  '${rmod['id']}'!='${rmod_id}'
      ${rmod_sn}  Set Variable  ${rmod['serialNumber']}
    END

    [Return]  ${rmod_sn}

RM Log All TX Antenna Lines Power
    [Arguments]  ${connection}  ${print_table}=${TRUE}
    [Documentation]
    ...  KW logs antenna lines power for all radio modules >= 5.1 via DAPD
    ...
    ...  | **Author:** mateusz.kawka@nokia.com
    ...
    ...  **Input Parameters:**
    ...
    ...  +------------------+------+-----------------------------------------------------+
    ...  | Parameter        | Man. | Description                                         |
    ...  +==================+======+=====================================================+
    ...  | print_table      | No   | print table with carriers power                     |
    ...  +------------------+------+-----------------------------------------------------+

    ${rmod_list}  admin.Get Parameters For All  class_name=RMOD  connection=${connection}
    FOR  ${rmod}  IN  @{rmod_list}
      Continue For Loop If  not '${rmod['productName']}'.startswith('A')
      Logging With Timestamp
      ...  TX antenna lines power for RMOD: ${rmod['productName']} with SN: ${rmod['serialNumber']}:
      radio.Get TX Pipes Power From DAPD
      ...  ru_serial_number=${rmod.serialNumber}
      ...  print_table=${print_table}
    END
